    "category": "Checkweigher",
    "type_designations": ["VersaWeigh", "VersaGP", "Versa RxC", "Versa RxM", "Versa Chain", "Teorema"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Mains-powered automatic checkweighing instrument (Category X). Constructions: VersaWeigh and VersaGP with the standard weighing system (VersaGP with integrated frame and adjustable-height supports); VersaWeigh and VersaGP alternatively with the Slack Conveyor non-powered weighing system; Versa RxC in stainless steel construction with the standard weighing system; Versa RxM and Versa Chain in stainless steel construction with the Slack Conveyor weighing system; Teorema with floor-standing frame conveyor and remote electrical cabinet with HMI. Devices: initial zero-setting, zero-tracking, automatic alarm device active during automatic operation (zero setting requested at least every 11 min), pre-set tare (subtractive), multi-range operation, static calibration not accessible to the user, dynamic calibration accessible to the user and recorded, internal memory for batch reports, device that acts upon significant faults, screen check at power-up. Interfaces: RS 232, USB, Ethernet, Parallel. Software: general software V312 Version 37.00.01.xx, legally relevant module 'MID Module' (shown in Menu/Tools/Versions); alternative software V312 Version 2.0 (37.00.02.xx) with selectable options for multi-lane, intermittent checkweigher (static-weigh; restricted to Slack Conveyor systems and Max <= 1500 g), data matrix, OEM and Teorema applications, and dedicated versions for Tare/Gross (39.00.01.xx), Multiproduct (41.00.01.xx) and Twin (42.00.01.xx) applications. Other load cell Emax values may be chosen provided sensitivity > 1 uV/e (Teorema: > 0.33 uV/div). Remote cabinets permitted for VersaWeigh and VersaGP provided the load cell is connected to the cabinet via metal conduit."
